            "review_title": "Review at SushiTakeAwayNhaTrang",
            "review_text": "Психолог333\n8 contributions\n0\nIt seemed expensive, tasteless, dirty\nSep 2026 • Family\nSaw it on Instagram in recommendations and went in. Very disappointed, an absolutely unacceptable price-quality combination. Overall, the impressions are quite weak, especially considering the price.\n\nWe ordered meat soup - completely ordinary, we could hardly taste it. Shrimp with rice - more or less, but also without any \"wow.\" They took a cut of raw fish - it looked not bad, but there was a little bit of it that was a bit scary, considering the overall impression of the establishment. We also ordered Philadelphia and other dishes. The octopus turned out to be completely tasteless and very rubbery in texture.\n\nThe worst thing is the condition of the establishment. The menu is dirty, overall the feeling is not of a clean and well-kept place. Even the curtains in the toilet looked dirty and grimy. The toilet itself, by the way, unexpectedly turned out to be normally cleaned—but the overall impression didn't save it.\n\nAnd all this for about 2 thousand rubles! For this amount, we expected a much nicer atmosphere and, most importantly, higher quality and tastier food.\n\nMaybe we just had bad luck with the dishes, but after this place was presented on Instagram almost as a gastronomic discovery, expectations and reality turned out to be very different.\n\nIf you are coming here based on enthusiastic recommendations from Instagram, I would advise lowering your expectations a bit.\nRead more\nTranslated from Russian\nShow original\nWritten September 11, 2026",
            "rating": 5.0,
            "review_date": "2026-10-11",
